{"entryId":"1674","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1674:1","sourceSha256":"b9858ca50ef6b3ecf77b4ae802d501714dcb8c36a83975426e73ac0d94d0566e","englishSha256":"13ca962b753b98816a8de37fbe0d5907b1eb79504f5f6f4f021727a810f60fdb","citations":[{"id":"1674:1:citation-01","he":[16,63],"en":[73,86],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_44a.3"},"reference":"Sanhedrin 44a:3","assessment":"The Bavli names R. Il’a transmitting two statements in the name of R. Yehudah bar Masparta, both about Achan.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 44a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_44a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 44a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_44a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1674:1:citation-02","he":[64,75],"en":[88,115],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_53.10"},"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 53:10","assessment":"Bereshit Rabbah gives R. Yudan bar Masparta directly, without Il’a, and the teaching concerns a royal feast. Distinguish the two attributions.","evidence":[{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 53:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_53.10"},"witness":"Midrash Rabbah -- TE"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[],"notes":[{"text":"The Bavli’s two teachings concern Achan. The Midrash’s Yudan bar Masparta interprets a royal banquet. Both checked texts use a rabbinic title in the passages, and the received Rav heading remains visible.","references":[],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 44a:3","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_44a.3"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 44a:4","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_44a.4"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Bereshit Rabbah 53:10","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Bereshit_Rabbah_53.10